        "execSummary":  "As enterprises scale AI beyond pilots, infrastructure cost models built on per-token pricing will systematically mislead budget planning because they ignore workload-specific GPU utilization, latency requirements, and demand elasticity. This matters directly for customer-support AI deployments, where real-time response latency is a service-level requirement ΓÇö a dimension that never appears on vendor pricing sheets but determines actual cost by an order of magnitude. The practical implication for procurement leaders is to reject vendor benchmarks conducted on generic workloads and insist on running your own production-representative traffic before signing infrastructure contracts. CoreWeave has an obvious commercial interest in this framing, but the underlying engineering argument is sound and independently verifiable.",
